WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.020
I'm Johan ten Hoeve,  I'm originally from Holland.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.680
I've been a clock maker and repairer for a last 12 years.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:20.280
So the process to make a wheel is by

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.740
having a wheel cast first, which we call a blank.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.800
You remove the skin of the blank

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.560
by filing it off or scraping it off.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.400
Once you've done that, you mark a centre hole or centre punch

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.720
and drill a hole in it.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:53.840
We use a dividing plate in order to set out the correct number of teeth onto the wheel.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:05.120
You then set out the teeth on the wheel with a device which allows you to mark or scribe lines on it.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:12.160
So if you have a wheel at 60 teeth you can mark 60 teeth onto the disc.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:24.240
Once you've put all the lines on it, you
file down beside the line.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.800
You cut out the gap in between the teeth.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:38.160
Finally, you shape the tips of the teeth and that's done by hand filing.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:48.160
And the last bit you do is file out the crossings, and that's kind of the process.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.800
When I cut the wheel and especially
when I, for instance, cut the teeth

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.160
you get into a flow and you get into a rhythm

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:05.360
and using the hand tools to shape the teeth or make the crossing,

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.880
is kind of like, an almost therapeutic way of working.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.160
You get into your own world and get lost in your work.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.440
What people always forget when you make something is how much time it takes.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.760
I can make a wheel in a day but then
that's only one wheel.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.720
If you want to make a whole clock, a year is kind of nothing.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.760
I always feel very satisfied when I finish a product or an item.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.640
You have more respect for things that have been handmade.

